    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41559" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπι-φρίσσω</span></b> , 
			Att.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπί-ττω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be rough</i> or <i>bristling on the
				surface,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαῖται νώτοις ἐπιπεφρίκασιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Emp.
					83.2
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φολίδεσσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.P.
					443
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σειληνοὺς πολιῇσιν -φρίσσοντας
				ἐθείραις</span> cj. in <i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				35.55
			</span></i> ; esp. of water, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέποδες..ἐπιφρίσσουσι γαλήνῃ</span>
			<i>make a ripple</i> on the calm sea, <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>C.</u>
				1.384
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>A.</u>
				1149
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				1.106
			</span></i>.</div>
